#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""milestone: the major milestones of a project, each with its own progress bar and ETA, in state.json and in Linear.

state.json `milestones` is an ordered list of
  {"id": "<slug>", "name": "...", "linear_id": "<Linear projectMilestone id>", "issues": ["ENG-1", ...],
   "added": "<date>", "origin": "plan" | "extension", "premortem": "<path>|null", "plan_review": "<path>|null"}
and state.json `blockers` ({issue: [issues that block it]}) is the one source of the dependency order: `recompute`
rebuilds `stages`, `critical_path` and `queue` from the milestone issue lists and the blockers. Blockers may cross
milestones. A state without `milestones` is one implicit milestone (the whole queue) and `bin/eta` prints its single
line as before. Ideas (state.json `ideas`, `bin/idea`) are never scheduled: their issues stay out of every scope here
and their Linear milestone never gets a target date.

  milestone list [--json]               id, name, done/total, ETA (from `bin/eta --json`)
  milestone seed <tickets.json>         after the plan's `bin/linear import`: one milestone per tickets.json milestone,
                                        blockers and sizes from the tickets, then recompute (the approved plan: no decision)
  milestone add <spec.json> [--dry-run] [--planner KEY] [--review-k N]
                [--skip-premortem "<why>"] [--skip-review "<why>"] [--approved --by <who> --source <kind:ref>]
  milestone adopt --id ID --name NAME --issues ENG-1,ENG-2,... [--linear-id ID | --create-linear]
                [--origin plan|extension] [--premortem PATH] [--plan-review PATH] --by <who> --source <kind:ref> [--dry-run]
  milestone recompute [--from-linear] [--dry-run]
  milestone sync [--decision D-n]... [--dry-run]
  milestone tidy [--dry-run]             delete empty milestones the plan dropped, archive empty autopilot projects, sync ticket states
  milestone proposed [--drop ID]         list (or drop) milestones drafted but not approved; bin/eta shows them
  milestone whatif --out PATH           state with every proposed milestone added (used by bin/eta)

add: extends a running project with a milestone, in this order, never skipping a step without a logged flag:
  a. validation (unknown dependencies, cycles, duplicate slugs, a KPI without target or measurement);
  b. pre-mortem of the milestone delta (`bin/premortem`, the existing PLAN.md as context) into
     .autopilot/plan/milestones/<id>/premortem.md;
  c. adversarial plan review of the milestone section (`bin/review`, POOL=plan_review) into .../plan-review.md;
  d. STOP, exit 3: the findings are printed for the owner and coordinator to fold into the spec. A second invocation
     with --approved --by <who> --source <kind:ref> continues (it stops again if b or c had to run in it);
  e. `bin/decision add` "milestone <name> added: N tickets", with that source;
  f. Linear: the projectMilestone, the issues and the blocks relations in the existing project (`bin/linear import`,
     checkpointed in .../tickets.created.json: a rerun never duplicates);
  g. the milestone section appended to PLAN.md, state.json updated (milestones, blockers, sizes, then recompute);
  g2. a spec with "from_ideas" (the skeleton `bin/idea promote` writes into .../milestones/<id>/spec.json): each idea is commented, linked as a duplicate of its
     new ticket (the tickets carrying its "from_idea", else the first ticket), moved to the Duplicate (else Canceled)
     state, struck through in the PLAN.md idea backlog and removed from state.json `ideas.issues`;
  h. `sync` with the decision, PLAN.md pushed as project content, the decision marked synced.
  Each step is recorded in .../status.json: rerunning the same command resumes after the last completed step.
  --dry-run validates and prints the stages and per-milestone ETAs the project would have, with no external call.
  --skip-premortem / --skip-review take the reason, which is written into status.json and the decision.
  A KPI or plan still marked TODO (a promoted idea's skeleton) is only a warning in --dry-run and refused otherwise.

spec.json:
  {"id": "whitebox", "name": "Whitebox + PR agents", "description": "one paragraph", "why": "one sentence",
   "kpis": [{"id": "K1", "kpi": "...", "target": "...", "measure": "command / query / count"}],
   "plan": "markdown: goal, architecture, rules and guardrails of this milestone",
   "tickets": [{"slug": "api", "title": "...", "description": "markdown", "estimate": 2 | "M", "priority": 2,
                "touches": ["purple/api/app.py", "web/src/components/drawer/"],
                "blocked_by": ["other-slug", "ENG-12", "slug-of-an-existing-ticket"], "labels": [], "from_idea": "ENG-40"}],
  Ticket shape (refused otherwise): estimate at most M (one concern, about 400 changed lines); `touches` lists
  the files or modules the ticket changes (max 8); two tickets that can run in parallel never change the same
  file outside tests/ and docs/ (order them with blocked_by or split by file).
   "from_ideas": ["ENG-40"]}   (optional: ideas promoted into this milestone, see g2)

adopt: groups tickets that already exist (a project planned before milestones, or a second plan already imported)
into a milestone: decision logged, then the Linear milestone linked (--linear-id), or created with the issues moved
into it (--create-linear, checkpointed), or none. Then run `recompute --from-linear` and `sync`.

recompute: blockers are the truth. --from-linear first reloads the blockers (and missing sizes) of every ticket in
scope from Linear. A state with no `blockers` at all is refused without --from-linear (it would flatten `stages`).

sync: sets each Linear milestone's target date to its ETA, runs tidy, then posts one project update with every
milestone bar (edits the previous one when it is less than 24 h old). --decision D-n (repeatable) adds that decision
to the update and marks it synced with the update's url. A tidy that changed something adds one line to that update
("tidy: 4 empty milestones removed, 1 project archived, 6 states updated").

tidy (also run by sync): 
  a. deletes this project's milestones that have no issues and are not in state.json `milestones` (matched by
     linear_id or name). Never the "Ideas (unscheduled)" milestone, never one with any issue.
  b. archives empty projects this autopilot created for the repo, excluding the current project. Creation is
     `project_created: true` on `.autopilot/plan/**/tickets.created.json` (that file's `project_id`, or
     `created_project_id` when a plan was folded into another project), a legacy reserved `pending` project id, or
     state.json `autopilot_project_ids`. An imported destination (`project_created: false`) is not evidence.
  c. ticket states follow state.json: `inflight` -> In Progress (else the team's started state), `done` -> Done
     (completed type), tickets waiting in `queue` or `stages` stay in an unstarted or backlog state. Only a state
     that differs is written. One line per change. --dry-run prints the same lines with a `would ` prefix and writes
     nothing.

Linear access: LINEAR_API_KEY, else the file named by state.json `linear_key_file`.
Exit: 0 ok; 1 invalid input or a failed step (rerun resumes); 2 a review step gave nothing usable (retry later);
3 needs approval.
"""
import argparse, datetime as dt, importlib.machinery, importlib.util, json, os, re, subprocess, sys, tempfile, uuid

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import autopilot_lib as lib

BIN = lib.HERE
IDENT = re.compile(r'^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*-\d+$')
SLUG = re.compile(r'^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$')
SML = {'XS': 0.5, 'S': 1.0, 'M': 2.0, 'L': 3.0, 'XL': 5.0}
NEEDS_APPROVAL = 3


def estimate(t):
    """A ticket's estimate as Linear takes it (a number), from a number or S/M/L."""
    u = units(t.get('estimate', 1))
    return int(u) if u == int(u) else u


def units(v):
    if isinstance(v, str) and v.strip().upper() in SML:
        return SML[v.strip().upper()]
    return float(v)


def die(msg, code=1):
    print(f'milestone: {msg}', file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(code)


def env(repo):
    e = dict(os.environ, AUTOPILOT_REPO=repo)
    key_file = lib.load_state(repo).get('linear_key_file')
    if not e.get('LINEAR_API_KEY') and key_file and os.path.exists(os.path.expanduser(key_file)):
        e['LINEAR_API_KEY'] = open(os.path.expanduser(key_file)).read().strip()
    return e


def linear(repo):
    """bin/linear as a module (its GraphQL helpers), with the API key resolved."""
    os.environ.update({k: v for k, v in env(repo).items() if k == 'LINEAR_API_KEY'})
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader('linear_cli', os.path.join(BIN, 'linear'))
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader('linear_cli', loader))
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def run(repo, cmd, extra_env=None, capture=True):
    p = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=capture, text=True, env=dict(env(repo), **(extra_env or {})), cwd=repo)
    return p.returncode, (p.stdout or ''), (p.stderr or '')


# ---------- schedule: stages, critical path, queue from milestone issue lists + blockers ----------

def idea_issues(st):
    return set((st.get('ideas') or {}).get('issues') or [])


def scope_of(st):
    ms = st.get('milestones') or []
    items = [t for m in ms for t in m.get('issues', [])] + list(st.get('queue', [])) + list(st.get('inflight', {}))
    if not ms:
        items = list(st.get('done', [])) + items
    ideas = idea_issues(st)  # never scheduled, whatever list they slipped into
    return [t for t in dict.fromkeys(items) if t not in ideas]


def find_cycle(nodes, deps):
    """A dependency cycle among `nodes` as a list, or None."""
    color, stack = {}, []

    def visit(t):
        color[t] = 1; stack.append(t)
        for b in deps.get(t, []):
            if b not in nodes: continue
            if color.get(b) == 1: return stack[stack.index(b):] + [b]
            if not color.get(b):
                c = visit(b)
                if c: return c
        color[t] = 2; stack.pop()
        return None

    for t in nodes:
        if not color.get(t):
            c = visit(t)
            if c: return c
    return None


def schedule(st):
    """(stages, critical_path, queue, warnings) for state `st`. Raises ValueError on a cycle."""
    done, inflight = set(st.get('done', [])), st.get('inflight', {})
    blockers, sizes = st.get('blockers', {}), st.get('sizes', {})
    scope = scope_of(st)
    inset = set(scope)
    warnings = sorted({f'{t} waits on {b}, outside every milestone and not done: counted as satisfied'
                       for t in scope for b in blockers.get(t, []) if b not in inset and b not in done})
    cyc = find_cycle(scope, blockers)
    if cyc: raise ValueError('dependency cycle: ' + ' -> '.join(cyc))
    open_ = [t for t in scope if t not in done]
    level = {}

    def lvl(t):
        if t not in level:
            ups = [lvl(b) for b in blockers.get(t, []) if b in inset and b not in done]
            level[t] = 1 + max(ups) if ups else 0
        return level[t]

    for t in open_: lvl(t)
    stages = [[t for t in open_ if level[t] == i] for i in range(max(level.values(), default=-1) + 1)]
    stages = [s for s in stages if s]
    queue = [t for s in stages for t in s if t not in inflight]
    longest = {}

    def chain(t):
        if t not in longest:
            ups = [chain(b) for b in blockers.get(t, []) if b in inset]
            best = max(ups, key=lambda c: c[0], default=(0.0, []))
            longest[t] = (best[0] + units(sizes.get(t, 1)), best[1] + [t])
        return longest[t]

    critical = max((chain(t) for t in scope), key=lambda c: c[0], default=(0.0, []))[1]
    return stages, critical, queue, warnings


def apply_schedule(st):
    stages, critical, queue, warnings = schedule(st)
    st['stages'], st['critical_path'], st['queue'] = stages, critical, queue
    return warnings


def show_schedule(stages, critical):
    for i, s in enumerate(stages, 1):
        print(f'  stage {i}: {", ".join(s)}')
    print(f'  critical path: {" -> ".join(critical) or "-"}')


# ---------- ETA (bin/eta --json is the one implementation) ----------

def eta(repo, state=None):
    extra = {'ETA_STATE': state} if state else {}
    rc, out, err = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'eta'), '--json'], extra)
    if rc != 0: die(f'bin/eta failed: {err.strip() or out.strip()}')
    return json.loads(out)


def bar(pct, width=20):
    return '█' * round(pct * width) + '░' * (width - round(pct * width))


def when(iso):
    return 'done' if not iso else dt.datetime.fromisoformat(iso).astimezone().strftime('%a %d %b %H:%M %Z')


def bars(e):
    rows = e['milestones'] or []
    w = max([len(r['name']) for r in rows] + [7])
    lines = [f"{r['name']:<{w}}  [{bar(r['pct'])}] {r['pct']:>4.0%}  {r['done']}/{r['total']} done  |  "
             + (f"ETA {when(r['end'])} (±{r['spread_min']} min)" if r['end'] else 'done') for r in rows]
    lines.append(f"{'Overall':<{w}}  [{bar(e['pct'])}] {e['pct']:>4.0%}  {e['done']} done, {e['inflight']} in flight, "
                 f"{e['todo']} to do  |  ETA {when(e['end'])} (±{e['spread_min']} min)")
    return lines


# ---------- spec validation and rendering ----------

def known_slugs(repo, skip=None):
    """slug -> identifier for every ticket already created from a tickets.json of this project (except under `skip`)."""
    out, base = {}, os.path.join(repo, '.autopilot')
    paths = []
    for root, _, files in os.walk(base):
        if root == skip: continue
        if 'tickets.created.json' in files and os.path.relpath(root, base).split(os.sep)[0].startswith('plan'):
            paths.append(os.path.join(root, 'tickets.created.json'))
    for p in sorted(paths):
        try:
            for slug, v in (lib.read_json(p).get('tickets') or {}).items():
                if v.get('identifier'): out.setdefault(slug, v['identifier'])
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass
    return out


def placeholders(spec):
    """Fields still marked TODO (the skeleton `bin/idea promote` writes): a plan cannot be approved with them."""
    out = [f'KPI {k.get("id") or "?"} {f}' for k in spec.get('kpis') or [] for f in ('kpi', 'target', 'measure')
           if str(k.get(f) or '').strip().upper().startswith('TODO')]
    if str(spec.get('plan') or '').strip().upper().startswith('TODO'): out.append('plan')
    out += [f'ticket {t.get("slug")} description' for t in spec.get('tickets') or []
            if str(t.get('description') or '').strip().upper().startswith('TODO')]
    return out


def validate(spec, st, repo, mid):
    """(errors, blocked_by resolved per slug: new slugs stay slugs, existing tickets become identifiers)."""
    errs, resolved = [], {}
    ideas = idea_issues(st)
    from_ideas = spec.get('from_ideas') or []
    errs += [f'from_ideas {t!r} is not an idea of this project (bin/idea list)' for t in from_ideas if t not in ideas]
    errs += [f'{t.get("slug")}: from_idea {t["from_idea"]!r} is not in from_ideas' for t in spec.get('tickets') or []
             if t.get('from_idea') and t['from_idea'] not in from_ideas]
    if not (spec.get('name') or '').strip(): errs.append('name is required')
    if not SLUG.match(mid): errs.append(f'id {mid!r} must be a lowercase slug')
    if any(m.get('id') == mid for m in st.get('milestones') or []): errs.append(f'milestone id {mid!r} already exists')
    if any(m.get('name') == spec.get('name') for m in st.get('milestones') or []): errs.append(f'milestone name {spec.get("name")!r} already exists')
    kpis = spec.get('kpis') or []
    if not kpis: errs.append('at least one KPI (kpi, target, measure) is required: no milestone without a measurable outcome')
    for k in kpis:
        miss = [f for f in ('kpi', 'target', 'measure') if not str(k.get(f) or '').strip()]
        if miss: errs.append(f'KPI {k.get("id") or k.get("kpi") or "?"} lacks {", ".join(miss)}')
    tickets = spec.get('tickets') or []
    if not tickets: errs.append('no tickets')
    slugs = [t.get('slug') for t in tickets]
    dup = sorted({s for s in slugs if slugs.count(s) > 1})
    if dup: errs.append(f'duplicate slugs {dup}')
    known = known_slugs(repo, skip=os.path.join(repo, '.autopilot', 'plan', 'milestones', mid))
    scope = set(scope_of(st)) | set(st.get('done', [])) | set(st.get('blockers', {}))
    if not st.get('blockers') and any(t not in st.get('done', []) for t in scope_of(st)):
        errs.append('state.json has no `blockers` for the open tickets: the stages could not be recomputed with the new '
                    'milestone. Load them first: bin/milestone recompute --from-linear')
    for t in tickets:
        s = t.get('slug') or ''
        if not SLUG.match(s): errs.append(f'slug {s!r} must be a lowercase slug')
        if s in known: errs.append(f'slug {s!r} already names {known[s]}')
        if not (t.get('title') or '').strip(): errs.append(f'{s}: title is required')
        try:
            if units(t.get('estimate', 1)) <= 0: raise ValueError
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            errs.append(f'{s}: estimate {t.get("estimate")!r} is not a number or S/M/L')
        out = []
        for b in t.get('blocked_by') or []:
            if b in slugs: out.append(b)
            elif IDENT.match(b) and b in scope: out.append(b)
            elif b in known: out.append(known[b])
            else: errs.append(f'{s}: blocked_by {b!r} is neither a slug of this spec nor a ticket of the project')
        resolved[s] = out
    cyc = find_cycle(slugs, resolved)
    if cyc: errs.append('dependency cycle: ' + ' -> '.join(cyc))
    else: errs += lib.ticket_shape_errors(tickets, {s: [b for b in resolved.get(s, []) if b in slugs] for s in slugs})
    return errs, resolved


def cell(s):
    return ' '.join(str(s or '').split()).replace('|', '\\|') or '-'


def render_section(spec, mid, ids=None, meta=None):
    ids = ids or {}
    lines = [f'### {spec["name"]} <!-- milestone:{mid} -->', '', spec.get('description', '').strip(), '']
    if meta: lines += [meta, '']
    lines += ['| # | KPI / acceptance | Target | How measured |', '|---|---|---|---|']
    lines += [f'| {cell(k.get("id") or f"K{i}")} | {cell(k["kpi"])} | {cell(k["target"])} | {cell(k["measure"])} |'
              for i, k in enumerate(spec.get('kpis') or [], 1)]
    if spec.get('plan'): lines += ['', spec['plan'].strip()]
    lines += ['', '| slug | issue | title | size | touches | blocked by |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
    for t in spec['tickets']:
        deps = ', '.join(ids.get(b, b) for b in t.get('blocked_by') or []) or '-'
        lines.append(f'| {t["slug"]} | {ids.get(t["slug"], "-")} | {cell(t["title"])} | {cell(t.get("estimate", 1))} | {cell(", ".join(t.get("touches") or []))} | {cell(deps)} |')
    return '\n'.join(lines).replace('\n\n\n', '\n\n') + '\n'


def insert_section(plan_text, mid, section):
    if f'<!-- milestone:{mid} -->' in plan_text: return plan_text
    lines = plan_text.splitlines()
    start = next((i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('## Milestones')), None)
    if start is not None:
        end = next((i for i in range(start + 1, len(lines)) if lines[i].startswith('## ')), len(lines))
    else:
        end = next((i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if re.match(r'## (Pre-mortem|Decision log|Approval)', l)), len(lines))
    lines[end:end] = section.rstrip('\n').splitlines() + ['']
    return '\n'.join(lines) + '\n'


def write_text(path, text):
    tmp = path + '.tmp'
    with open(tmp, 'w') as f: f.write(text)
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def what_if(st, mid, spec, resolved, ids):
    """A copy of the state with the milestone added (tickets named by `ids`), stages recomputed."""
    w = json.loads(json.dumps(st))
    issues = [ids[t['slug']] for t in spec['tickets']]
    if not w.get('milestones'):
        w['milestones'] = [{'id': 'current', 'name': w.get('project') or 'Current scope', 'issues': scope_of(w)}]
    w['milestones'].append({'id': mid, 'name': spec['name'], 'issues': issues})
    w.setdefault('blockers', {}); w.setdefault('sizes', {})
    for t in spec['tickets']:
        w['blockers'][ids[t['slug']]] = [ids.get(b, b) for b in resolved[t['slug']]]
        w['sizes'][ids[t['slug']]] = units(t.get('estimate', 1))
    return w


# ---------- proposed milestones (visible in bin/eta before approval) ----------

def propose(repo, mid, spec_path, name):
    """Mark a drafted milestone as proposed: bin/eta shows it (awaiting approval) until it is approved or dropped."""
    def fn(s):
        if any(m.get('id') == mid for m in s.get('milestones') or []): return
        s.setdefault('proposed_milestones', {})[mid] = {'name': name, 'spec': os.path.abspath(spec_path),
                                                        'at': lib.now().isoformat()}
    lib.update_state(repo, fn)


def whatif_proposed(repo, st):
    """The state with every proposed milestone added (tickets as +slug), stages recomputed; None without proposals."""
    props = {k: v for k, v in (st.get('proposed_milestones') or {}).items()
             if not any(m.get('id') == k for m in st.get('milestones') or [])}
    if not props: return None
    w = json.loads(json.dumps(st)); w.pop('proposed_milestones', None)
    for mid, p in props.items():
        try: spec = lib.read_json(p['spec'])
        except (OSError, ValueError): continue
        status_path = os.path.join(repo, '.autopilot', 'plan', 'milestones', mid, 'status.json')
        status = lib.read_json(status_path) if os.path.exists(status_path) else {}
        resolved = status.get('resolved')
        if not resolved:
            errs, resolved = validate(spec, st, repo, mid)
            if errs: continue
        ids = {t['slug']: '+' + t['slug'] for t in spec['tickets']}
        w = what_if(w, mid, spec, resolved, ids)
        w['milestones'][-1]['proposed'] = True
    apply_schedule(w)
    return w


def cmd_whatif(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo(); w = whatif_proposed(repo, lib.load_state(repo))
    if w is None: sys.exit(4)
    lib.write_json_atomic(a.out, w)


def cmd_proposed(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo()
    if a.drop:
        lib.update_state(repo, lambda s: (s.get('proposed_milestones') or {}).pop(a.drop, None)); print(f'dropped {a.drop}'); return
    for mid, p in (lib.load_state(repo).get('proposed_milestones') or {}).items():
        print(f"{mid:<16} {p['name']:<40} proposed {p['at'][:16]}  {p['spec']}")


# ---------- commands ----------

def cmd_list(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo(); e = eta(repo)
    if a.json: print(json.dumps(e['milestones'], indent=1)); return
    for r in e['milestones'] or []:
        print(f"{r['id']:<16} {r['name']:<32} {r['done']}/{r['total']} done  "
              + (f"ETA {when(r['end'])} (±{r['spread_min']} min)" if r['end'] else 'done'))
    if not e['milestones']:
        print(f"(no milestones: one implicit scope) {e['done']} done, {e['todo']} to do  ETA {when(e['end'])}")


def cmd_add(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo(); st = lib.load_state(repo)
    try: spec = lib.read_json(a.spec)
    except (OSError, ValueError) as ex: die(f'cannot read {a.spec}: {ex}')
    mid = spec.get('id') or re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', (spec.get('name') or '').lower()).strip('-')
    d = os.path.join(repo, '.autopilot', 'plan', 'milestones', mid)
    status_path = os.path.join(d, 'status.json')
    status = lib.read_json(status_path) if os.path.exists(status_path) else {}

    def save():
        os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True); status['at'] = lib.now().isoformat(); lib.write_json_atomic(status_path, status)

    if status.get('synced'):
        print(f'milestone {mid}: already added ({status.get("decision")}, {status["synced"]})'); return
    applied = bool(status.get('state'))  # past step g: the milestone is in state.json already
    if not applied:
        errs, resolved = validate(spec, st, repo, mid)
        if errs:
            for e in errs: print(f'INVALID: {e}')
            sys.exit(1)
        status['resolved'] = resolved
    resolved = status['resolved']
    if not applied and not a.approved:
        propose(repo, mid, a.spec, spec['name'])  # bin/eta shows it as proposed until approval or `milestone proposed --drop`
    if a.dry_run:
        ids = {t['slug']: '+' + t['slug'] for t in spec['tickets']}
        w = what_if(st, mid, spec, resolved, ids)
        try: warnings = apply_schedule(w)
        except ValueError as ex: die(str(ex))
        print(f'valid: milestone {spec["name"]!r} ({mid}), {len(spec["tickets"])} tickets, '
              f'{sum(units(t.get("estimate", 1)) for t in spec["tickets"]):g} size units (new tickets shown as +slug)')
        for x in placeholders(spec): print(f'  warning: {x} is still TODO: fill it before the real add')
        show_schedule(w['stages'], w['critical_path'])
        for x in warnings: print(f'  warning: {x}')
        with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile('w', suffix='.json', delete=False) as f:
            json.dump(w, f)
        try: e = eta(repo, f.name)
        finally: os.unlink(f.name)
        print('ETA with this milestone:')
        for line in bars(e): print('  ' + line)
        print('dry run: no pre-mortem, review, decision, Linear, PLAN.md or state change')
        return
    if a.approved and not (a.by and a.source): die('--approved needs --by <who> and --source <kind:ref>')
    todo = [] if applied else placeholders(spec)
    if todo: die(f'still TODO in {a.spec}: {", ".join(todo)}. Fill them (measurable KPIs, the plan, ticket instructions) first')
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    digest = lib.digest_text(json.dumps(spec, sort_keys=True))
    section = render_section(spec, mid)
    write_text(os.path.join(d, 'section.md'), section)
    plan_path = os.environ.get('AUTOPILOT_PLAN') or os.path.join(repo, 'PLAN.md')
    if not os.path.exists(plan_path): die(f'{plan_path} not found: the milestone section and its decision go there')
    planner = a.planner or st.get('coordinator')
    ran_review_now = False
    # A spec edited before approval (findings folded in) is the expected flow; a spec edited and run again WITHOUT
    # --approved asks for a new review round of the new delta.
    stale = not a.approved and status.get('reviewed_digest') not in (None, digest)
    if not applied and (stale or not status.get('premortem')):
        if a.skip_premortem:
            status['premortem'] = {'skipped': a.skip_premortem}
        else:
            if not planner: die('no planner: pass --planner <roster key> or set `coordinator` in state.json')
            ctx = open(plan_path).read()
            write_text(os.path.join(d, 'premortem-input.md'),
                       f'# Pre-mortem scope: milestone "{spec["name"]}", added to a running project\n\n'
                       'Only the milestone below is under review. The existing plan after the separator is context: it was '
                       'already pre-mortem\'d and is being executed. Raise a reason about it only when this milestone makes '
                       'it fail (shared files, a dependency, a KPI it moves, the deadline).\n\n'
                       f'{section}\n---\n\n# Existing plan (context)\n\n{ctx}')
            cmd = [os.path.join(BIN, 'premortem'), os.path.join(d, 'premortem-input.md'), '--repo', repo,
                   '--planner', planner, '--out-dir', d]
            print(f'pre-mortem of milestone {mid} (10-40 min) ...', flush=True)
            rc, out, err = run(repo, cmd)
            open(os.path.join(d, 'premortem.log'), 'w').write(out + err)
            if rc == 2 or not os.path.exists(os.path.join(d, 'premortem.md')):
                print(out[-1500:] + err[-500:]); die('pre-mortem gave no usable result (see premortem.log); rerun later', 2)
            status['premortem'] = {'path': os.path.join(d, 'premortem.md'), 'exit': rc, 'degraded': rc == 1}
            ran_review_now = True
        status['reviewed_digest'] = digest; save()
    if not applied and (stale or not status.get('review')):
        if a.skip_review:
            status['review'] = {'skipped': a.skip_review}
        else:
            n = status.get('review_round', 0) + 1
            inp = os.path.join(d, f'review-input-{n}.md')
            write_text(inp, f'# Milestone {spec["name"]} (extension of a running project)\n\n'
                            f'Review this milestone plan as an addition to {plan_path} (read it: the existing plan is '
                            'being executed). Check it fits the existing architecture, tickets and KPIs, that its '
                            'dependencies on existing tickets are real and complete, and that its KPIs are measurable. '
                            'Check that every ticket is atomic: one concern, at most about 400 changed lines, a '
                            '`touches` list that matches what the instructions really change, and no two tickets that '
                            'can run in parallel changing the same file (including files that tickets already in '
                            'flight change). A ticket that is too big or shares a hot file is a major finding: name the '
                            'split.\n\n'
                            + section)
            rc, brief, err = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'mkbrief'), 'plan', f'milestone-{mid}', f'm{n}', inp])
            if rc != 0: die(f'mkbrief failed: {err.strip()}')
            extra = {'POOL': 'plan_review'}
            if a.planner and a.planner != st.get('coordinator'):
                reg = lib.load_reg(); ad = lib.adapters(); m = reg['models'].get(a.planner) or die(f'unknown planner {a.planner}')
                extra['EXCLUDE'] = a.planner; extra['EXCLUDE_VENDOR'] = lib.vendor_of(m, ad.get(m['cli']))
            print(f'plan review of milestone {mid} ...', flush=True)
            rc, out, err = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'review'), f'milestone-{mid}', f'm{n}', brief.strip(), str(a.review_k)], extra)
            status['review_round'] = n
            if rc in (2, 3):
                print(out[-1500:] + err[-500:]); save(); die('plan review gave no usable verdict; rerun later', 2)
            path = os.path.join(d, 'plan-review.md')
            write_text(path, f'# Plan review of milestone {spec["name"]}, round m{n}: '
                             f'{"approve" if rc == 0 else "changes required"}\n\n{out}')
            status['review'] = {'path': path, 'exit': rc, 'verdict': 'approve' if rc == 0 else 'changes_required'}
            ran_review_now = True
        status['reviewed_digest'] = digest; save()
    if not applied and (ran_review_now or not a.approved):
        print(f'NEEDS APPROVAL: milestone {spec["name"]!r} ({mid}), {len(spec["tickets"])} tickets')
        for k in ('premortem', 'review'):
            s = status[k]
            print(f'--- {k}: ' + (f'SKIPPED ({s["skipped"]})' if s.get('skipped') else s['path'] + (' DEGRADED' if s.get('degraded') else '')))
            if not s.get('skipped'): print(open(s['path']).read().rstrip())
        print(f'---\nFold the findings into {a.spec} (each accepted reason gets a guardrail with a home: a KPI, a check, a '
              'ticket, a rule; a rejected one is logged with its evidence), show them to the owner, then rerun with\n'
              f'  --approved --by <owner> --source user:"<their approval, quoted>"')
        sys.exit(NEEDS_APPROVAL)
    # e. decision
    if not status.get('decision'):
        skipped = [f'{k} skipped: {status[k]["skipped"]}' for k in ('premortem', 'review') if status[k].get('skipped')]
        why = '; '.join([spec.get('why') or (spec.get('description') or '').split('. ')[0]] + skipped).strip('; ')
        rc, out, err = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'decision'), 'add', '--change', f'milestone {spec["name"]} added: {len(spec["tickets"])} tickets',
                                  '--source', a.source, '--by', a.by, '--why', why,
                                  '--affects', ', '.join([mid] + [t['slug'] for t in spec['tickets']] + list(spec.get('from_ideas') or []))])
        if rc != 0: die(f'decision refused: {err.strip() or out.strip()}')
        status['decision'] = out.split()[0]; status['approved'] = {'by': a.by, 'source': a.source, 'digest': digest}; save()
    # f. Linear
    tickets_path = os.path.join(d, 'tickets.json')
    if not status.get('linear'):
        if not st.get('project_id') or st['project_id'].startswith('<') or not st.get('team'):
            die('state.json has no project_id/team: a milestone extends an existing Linear project')
        lib.write_json_atomic(tickets_path, {
            'project': {'name': st.get('project', '')},
            'milestones': [{'name': spec['name'], 'description': spec.get('description', '')}],
            'tickets': [dict({k: v for k, v in t.items() if k != 'blocked_by'}, milestone=spec['name'],
                             estimate=estimate(t),
                             blocked_by=resolved[t['slug']]) for t in spec['tickets']]})
        rc, out, err = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'linear'), 'import', tickets_path, '--team', st['team'], '--project-id', st['project_id']], capture=False)
        if rc != 0: die('Linear import failed; rerun the same command to resume from the checkpoint')
        status['linear'] = True; save()
    created = lib.read_json(os.path.join(d, 'tickets.created.json'))
    ids = {s: v['identifier'] for s, v in created['tickets'].items()}
    # g. PLAN.md + state
    if not status.get('state'):
        meta = (f'Added {dt.date.today().isoformat()} as an extension ({status["decision"]}). '
                + ' · '.join(f'{label}: ' + (f'skipped ({status[k]["skipped"]})' if status[k].get('skipped') else f'`{os.path.relpath(status[k]["path"], repo)}`')
                             for k, label in (('premortem', 'Pre-mortem'), ('review', 'plan review'))))
        write_text(plan_path, insert_section(open(plan_path).read(), mid, render_section(spec, mid, ids, meta)))

        def fn(s):
            s.setdefault('milestones', [])
            if not any(m['id'] == mid for m in s['milestones']):
                if not s['milestones'] and scope_of(s):
                    s['milestones'].append({'id': 'current', 'name': s.get('project') or 'Current scope', 'linear_id': None,
                                            'issues': scope_of(s), 'added': None, 'origin': 'plan',
                                            'premortem': None, 'plan_review': None})
                s['milestones'].append({'id': mid, 'name': spec['name'], 'linear_id': created['milestones'].get(spec['name']),
                                        'issues': [ids[t['slug']] for t in spec['tickets']], 'added': dt.date.today().isoformat(),
                                        'origin': 'extension', 'premortem': status['premortem'].get('path'),
                                        'plan_review': status['review'].get('path')})
            s.setdefault('blockers', {}); s.setdefault('sizes', {})
            for t in spec['tickets']:
                s['blockers'][ids[t['slug']]] = [ids.get(b, b) for b in resolved[t['slug']]]
                s['sizes'][ids[t['slug']]] = units(t.get('estimate', 1))
            (s.get('proposed_milestones') or {}).pop(mid, None)
            return apply_schedule(s)

        for x in lib.update_state(repo, fn): print(f'warning: {x}')
        status['state'] = True; save()
    # g2. promoted ideas leave the backlog, closed as duplicates of the new tickets
    for idea in spec.get('from_ideas') or []:
        if idea in status.setdefault('ideas_closed', []): continue
        rid = status.setdefault('idea_relations', {}).setdefault(idea, str(uuid.uuid4())); save()
        close_idea(repo, idea, spec, ids, plan_path, status['decision'], rid)
        status['ideas_closed'].append(idea); save()
    # h. Linear content + milestone bars + decision mirrored
    lin = linear(repo)
    lin.cmd_project_content([st['project_id'], plan_path])
    status['synced'] = do_sync(repo, [status['decision']]); save()
    print(f'milestone {mid} added: {", ".join(ids[t["slug"]] for t in spec["tickets"])} ({status["decision"]}, {status["synced"]})')


def close_idea(repo, idea, spec, ids, plan_path, decision, rid):
    """Idea `idea`, promoted into the milestone of `spec`: duplicate relation to its first new ticket (client id `rid`,
    checkpointed by the caller), state Duplicate (else the team's first canceled state), a comment, struck through in
    PLAN.md, out of state.json `ideas.issues`. A rerun after a crash repeats at most the comment."""
    lin = linear(repo)
    targets = [ids[t['slug']] for t in spec['tickets'] if t.get('from_idea') == idea] or [ids[spec['tickets'][0]['slug']]]
    i = lin.issue(idea)
    lin.retry(lin.relate, i['id'], lin.issue(targets[0])['id'], 'duplicate', rid)
    lin.retry(lin.update_issue, i['id'], {'stateId': lin.state_id(i['team']['id'], 'Duplicate', 'canceled')})
    lin.comment(i['id'], f'Promoted into milestone **{spec["name"]}** ({decision}): {", ".join(targets)}. '
                         'Closed as a duplicate; the work is tracked there.')
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader('idea_cli', os.path.join(BIN, 'idea'))
    idea_mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader('idea_cli', loader)); loader.exec_module(idea_mod)
    write_text(plan_path, idea_mod.mark_promoted(open(plan_path).read(), idea, f'promoted to {spec["name"]} ({", ".join(targets)})'))

    def fn(s):
        lst = (s.get('ideas') or {}).get('issues') or []
        if idea in lst: lst.remove(idea)
    lib.update_state(repo, fn)
    print(f'idea {idea} closed as a duplicate of {targets[0]}')


def cmd_seed(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo()
    spec = lib.read_json(a.tickets)
    cpath = a.tickets.rsplit('.', 1)[0] + '.created.json'
    if not os.path.exists(cpath): die(f'{cpath} not found: create the Linear project first (bin/linear import)')
    created = lib.read_json(cpath)
    ids = {s_: v['identifier'] for s_, v in created['tickets'].items()}
    missing = [t['slug'] for t in spec['tickets'] if t['slug'] not in ids]
    if missing: die(f'tickets not created in Linear yet: {missing}')
    pm = os.path.join(repo, '.autopilot', 'plan', 'premortem.md')
    ms = []
    for m in spec.get('milestones') or []:
        mid = m.get('id') or re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', m['name'].lower()).strip('-')
        ms.append({'id': mid, 'name': m['name'], 'linear_id': created['milestones'].get(m['name']),
                   'issues': [ids[t['slug']] for t in spec['tickets'] if t.get('milestone') == m['name']],
                   'added': dt.date.today().isoformat(), 'origin': 'plan', 'premortem': pm if os.path.exists(pm) else None,
                   'plan_review': None})

    def fn(s):
        if s.get('milestones'): raise ValueError('state.json already has milestones: use add or adopt')
        s['milestones'] = ms; s.setdefault('blockers', {}); s.setdefault('sizes', {})
        for t in spec['tickets']:
            s['blockers'][ids[t['slug']]] = [ids.get(b, b) for b in t.get('blocked_by') or []]
            s['sizes'].setdefault(ids[t['slug']], units(t.get('estimate', 1)))
            if ids[t['slug']] not in s.get('done', []) and ids[t['slug']] not in s.setdefault('queue', []):
                s['queue'].append(ids[t['slug']])
        return apply_schedule(s)

    try: warnings = lib.update_state(repo, fn)
    except ValueError as ex: die(str(ex))
    for x in warnings: print(f'warning: {x}')
    s = lib.load_state(repo)
    print(f'{len(ms)} milestones, {len(spec["tickets"])} tickets')
    show_schedule(s['stages'], s['critical_path'])


def cmd_adopt(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo(); st = lib.load_state(repo)
    issues = list(dict.fromkeys(i.strip() for i in a.issues.split(',') if i.strip()))
    errs = []
    if not SLUG.match(a.id): errs.append(f'id {a.id!r} must be a lowercase slug')
    if any(m.get('id') == a.id for m in st.get('milestones') or []): errs.append(f'milestone {a.id} already exists')
    taken = {t: m['id'] for m in st.get('milestones') or [] for t in m.get('issues', [])}
    errs += [f'{t} already belongs to milestone {taken[t]}' for t in issues if t in taken]
    errs += [f'{t} is not an issue identifier' for t in issues if not IDENT.match(t)]
    errs += [f'{t} is an idea: promote it (bin/idea promote), then bin/milestone add' for t in issues if t in idea_issues(st)]
    if a.linear_id and a.linear_id == (st.get('ideas') or {}).get('linear_milestone_id'):
        errs.append('--linear-id is the Ideas milestone: ideas are never scheduled')
    if not issues: errs.append('no issues')
    if a.linear_id and a.create_linear: errs.append('--linear-id and --create-linear are exclusive')
    if errs:
        for e in errs: print(f'INVALID: {e}')
        sys.exit(1)
    if a.dry_run:
        print(f'valid: milestone {a.name!r} ({a.id}) over {len(issues)} existing tickets; Linear: '
              + (f'link {a.linear_id}' if a.linear_id else 'create the milestone and move the issues' if a.create_linear else 'none'))
        return
    d = os.path.join(repo, '.autopilot', 'plan', 'milestones', a.id); os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    cp = os.path.join(d, 'adopt.json')
    ck = lib.read_json(cp) if os.path.exists(cp) else {'moved': []}
    if not ck.get('decision'):
        rc, out, err = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'decision'), 'add', '--change', f'milestone {a.name} defined over {len(issues)} existing tickets',
                                  '--source', a.source, '--by', a.by, '--why', a.why or 'group the existing tickets under a major milestone with its own ETA',
                                  '--affects', ', '.join([a.id] + issues)])
        if rc != 0: die(f'decision refused: {err.strip() or out.strip()}')
        ck['decision'] = out.split()[0]; lib.write_json_atomic(cp, ck)
    lid = a.linear_id
    if a.create_linear:
        lin = linear(repo); pid = st.get('project_id') or die('state.json has no project_id')
        if not ck.get('linear_id'):
            ck['linear_id'] = ck.get('pending') or str(uuid.uuid4()); ck['pending'] = ck['linear_id']; lib.write_json_atomic(cp, ck)
            lin.create_milestone(pid, a.name, a.description or '', ck['linear_id'])
        lid = ck['linear_id']
        for t in issues:
            if t in ck['moved']: continue
            lin.move_issue(t, pid, lid); ck['moved'].append(t); lib.write_json_atomic(cp, ck)
            print(f'moved {t} into {a.name}')

    def fn(s):
        s.setdefault('milestones', [])
        if any(m['id'] == a.id for m in s['milestones']): return
        s['milestones'].append({'id': a.id, 'name': a.name, 'linear_id': lid, 'issues': issues, 'added': dt.date.today().isoformat(),
                                'origin': a.origin, 'premortem': a.premortem, 'plan_review': a.plan_review})

    lib.update_state(repo, fn)
    print(f'milestone {a.id} adopted ({ck["decision"]}). Next: bin/milestone recompute --from-linear --dry-run, then without --dry-run; bin/milestone sync --decision {ck["decision"]}')


def cmd_recompute(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo(); st = lib.load_state(repo)
    fetched = {}
    if a.from_linear:
        lin = linear(repo)
        for t in scope_of(st):
            fetched[t] = lin.issue_links(t)
        print(f'loaded blockers of {len(fetched)} tickets from Linear')
    elif not st.get('blockers'):
        die('state.json has no `blockers`: recompute would flatten `stages`. Load them: bin/milestone recompute --from-linear')

    def fn(s):
        s.setdefault('blockers', {}); s.setdefault('sizes', {})
        for t, f in fetched.items():
            s['blockers'][t] = f['blockers']
            if t not in s['sizes'] and f.get('estimate'): s['sizes'][t] = f['estimate']
        before = (s.get('stages'), s.get('critical_path'))
        warnings = apply_schedule(s)
        return before, warnings

    if a.dry_run:
        w = json.loads(json.dumps(st)); before, warnings = fn(w); s = w
    else:
        try: before, warnings = lib.update_state(repo, fn)
        except ValueError as ex: die(str(ex))
        s = lib.load_state(repo)
    for x in warnings: print(f'warning: {x}')
    print(f'{len(before[0] or [])} stages -> {len(s["stages"])} stages{" (dry run, not saved)" if a.dry_run else ""}')
    show_schedule(s['stages'], s['critical_path'])


def autopilot_project_ids(repo, st):
    """Return projects with evidence of creation by this autopilot, never mere import destinations.

    `project_created: true` is that evidence (`bin/linear import`, or the MCP checkpoint documented in
    autopilot-plan step 7). When the plan is folded into another project, `project_id` may name the
    destination and `created_project_id` keeps the project this autopilot created: only the latter is
    a candidate. A missing flag still counts for a legacy reserved `pending` project id. `project_created:
    false` is an imported destination and is ignored.
    """
    ids = set(st.get('autopilot_project_ids') or [])
    base = os.path.join(repo, '.autopilot', 'plan')
    for root, _, files in os.walk(base):
        if 'tickets.created.json' not in files:
            continue
        try:
            ck = lib.read_json(os.path.join(root, 'tickets.created.json'))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        pid = ck.get('project_id')
        created_pid = ck.get('created_project_id')
        reserved = [v for k, v in (ck.get('pending') or {}).items() if k.startswith('project:')]
        flag = ck.get('project_created')
        if flag is True:
            src = created_pid or pid
            if isinstance(src, str) and src:
                ids.add(src)
        elif flag is not False and isinstance(pid, str) and pid in reserved:
            ids.add(pid)
    return sorted(x for x in ids if isinstance(x, str) and x and not x.startswith('<'))


def tidy_summary(nm, np, ns):
    ms = 'empty milestone' if nm == 1 else 'empty milestones'
    pr = 'project' if np == 1 else 'projects'
    stt = 'state' if ns == 1 else 'states'
    return 'tidy: %d %s removed, %d %s archived, %d %s updated' % (nm, ms, np, pr, ns, stt)


def tidy(repo, dry=False):
    """Delete empty dropped milestones, archive empty autopilot projects, and move ticket states to match state.json.
    Returns (summary line, (milestones, projects, states)). Prints one line per change; --dry-run writes nothing."""
    st = lib.load_state(repo)
    lin = linear(repo)
    pid = st.get('project_id')
    say = lambda msg: print(('would ' if dry else '') + msg)
    nm = np = ns = 0
    ideas = st.get('ideas') or {}
    idea_ids = {ideas.get('linear_milestone_id')} - {None, ''}
    idea_names = {ideas.get('name') or 'Ideas (unscheduled)', 'Ideas (unscheduled)'}
    kept_ids = {m.get('linear_id') for m in st.get('milestones') or [] if m.get('linear_id')}
    kept_names = {m.get('name') for m in st.get('milestones') or [] if m.get('name')}
    if pid and not str(pid).startswith('<'):
        for m in lin.milestones_detailed(pid):
            if m['id'] in idea_ids or m['name'] in idea_names or m['id'] in kept_ids or m['name'] in kept_names or not m['empty']:
                continue
            say('remove empty milestone %s (%s)' % (m['name'], m['id']))
            if not dry:
                lin.delete_milestone(m['id'])
            nm += 1
        for opid in autopilot_project_ids(repo, st):
            if opid == pid:
                continue
            status = lin.project_status(opid)
            if not status or status['archived'] or status['issues']:
                continue
            say('archive project %s' % opid)
            if not dry:
                lin.archive_project(opid)
            np += 1
        done = set(st.get('done') or [])
        inflight = set((st.get('inflight') or {}).keys())
        waiting = set(st.get('queue') or [])
        for stage in st.get('stages') or []:
            waiting.update(stage or [])
        waiting -= done | inflight
        if st.get('team') and (done or inflight or waiting):
            states = lin.states_of(lin.team(st['team'])['id'])
            by_ident = {i['identifier']: i for i in lin.project_issues(pid, with_relations=False)}

            def target(ident):
                if ident in done:
                    return lin.pick_state(states, 'Done', 'completed')
                if ident in inflight:
                    return lin.pick_state(states, 'In Progress', 'started')
                cur = (by_ident.get(ident) or {}).get('state') or {}
                if cur.get('type') in ('unstarted', 'backlog'):
                    return None
                return lin.pick_state(states, 'Todo', 'unstarted')

            for ident in sorted(done | inflight | waiting):
                i = by_ident.get(ident)
                tgt = target(ident) if i else None
                if not i or not tgt:
                    continue
                cur = i.get('state') or {}
                if cur.get('id') == tgt['id'] or (cur.get('name') or '').lower() == tgt['name'].lower():
                    continue
                say('%s: %s -> %s' % (ident, cur.get('name') or '?', tgt['name']))
                if not dry:
                    lin.update_issue(i['id'], {'stateId': tgt['id']})
                ns += 1
    line = tidy_summary(nm, np, ns)
    if nm or np or ns:
        say(line)
    return line, (nm, np, ns)


def sync_body(e, decisions=(), repo=None):
    lines = ['**Milestones** (`bin/eta`, ' + dt.datetime.now().astimezone().strftime('%a %d %b %H:%M %Z') + ')', '', '```']
    lines += bars(e) + ['```']
    if e.get('replan'): lines += ['', 'Re-plan signals: ' + '; '.join(e['replan'])]
    if decisions and repo:
        rc, out, _ = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'decision'), 'list'])
        lines.append('')
        for dn in decisions:
            row = next((re.sub(r'\s+\[[^\]]*\]\s+', '  ', l, count=1) for l in out.splitlines() if l.startswith(dn + ' ')), dn)
            lines.append(f'Decision {row}')
    return '\n'.join(lines) + '\n'


def do_sync(repo, decisions=(), dry=False):
    st = lib.load_state(repo); e = eta(repo)
    ms = {m['id']: m for m in st.get('milestones') or []}
    targets = {}
    for r in e['milestones'] or []:
        m = ms.get(r['id'])
        if m and m.get('linear_id') and r['end'] and m['linear_id'] != (st.get('ideas') or {}).get('linear_milestone_id'):
            date = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(r['end']).date().isoformat()
            if m.get('target_date') != date: targets[r['id']] = date
    body = sync_body(e, decisions, repo)
    n_ideas = len((st.get('ideas') or {}).get('issues') or [])
    if n_ideas:
        body += f'\n{(st.get("ideas") or {}).get("name") or "Ideas (unscheduled)"}: {n_ideas} ideas, not scheduled (`bin/idea list`)\n'
    line, counts = tidy(repo, dry=dry)
    if any(counts):
        body += '\n' + line + '\n'
    prev = st.get('milestone_update') or {}
    fresh = prev.get('id') and (lib.now() - lib.parse_time(prev['at'])).total_seconds() < 24 * 3600
    if dry:
        for mid, date in targets.items(): print(f'would set {ms[mid]["name"]} target date {date}')
        print(('would edit project update ' + prev['id'] if fresh else 'would post a project update') + ':\n' + body)
        return None
    lin = linear(repo)
    for mid, date in targets.items():
        lin.set_target_date(ms[mid]['linear_id'], date); print(f'{ms[mid]["name"]}: target date {date}')
    up = lin.upsert_project_update(st['project_id'], body, prev['id'] if fresh else None)

    def fn(s):
        for m in s.get('milestones') or []:
            if m['id'] in targets: m['target_date'] = targets[m['id']]
        s['milestone_update'] = {'id': up['id'], 'url': up.get('url'), 'at': prev['at'] if fresh else lib.now().isoformat()}

    lib.update_state(repo, fn)
    print(f'project update {"edited" if fresh else "posted"}: {up.get("url")}')
    for dn in decisions:
        rc, out, err = run(repo, [os.path.join(BIN, 'decision'), 'synced', dn, up.get('url') or up['id']])
        if rc != 0: die(f'decision synced {dn} failed: {err.strip()}')
    return up.get('url') or up['id']


def cmd_sync(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo(); st = lib.load_state(repo)
    if not st.get('project_id') or st['project_id'].startswith('<'): die('state.json has no project_id')
    do_sync(repo, a.decision or [], a.dry_run)


def cmd_tidy(a):
    repo = lib.find_repo(); st = lib.load_state(repo)
    if not st.get('project_id') or st['project_id'].startswith('<'): die('state.json has no project_id')
    line, counts = tidy(repo, dry=a.dry_run)
    if a.dry_run or not any(counts):
        return
    linear(repo).upsert_project_update(st['project_id'], line + '\n')


def main():
    if len(sys.argv) < 2 or sys.argv[1] in ('-h', '--help'): print(__doc__); sys.exit(0 if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 1)
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='milestone'); sub = p.add_subparsers(dest='cmd')
    li = sub.add_parser('list'); li.add_argument('--json', action='store_true')
    ad = sub.add_parser('add'); ad.add_argument('spec'); ad.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true')
    ad.add_argument('--planner'); ad.add_argument('--review-k', type=int, default=1)
    ad.add_argument('--skip-premortem', metavar='WHY'); ad.add_argument('--skip-review', metavar='WHY')
    ad.add_argument('--approved', action='store_true'); ad.add_argument('--by'); ad.add_argument('--source')
    se = sub.add_parser('seed'); se.add_argument('tickets')
    ao = sub.add_parser('adopt'); ao.add_argument('--id', required=True); ao.add_argument('--name', required=True)
    ao.add_argument('--issues', required=True); ao.add_argument('--linear-id'); ao.add_argument('--create-linear', action='store_true')
    ao.add_argument('--description'); ao.add_argument('--why')
    ao.add_argument('--origin', choices=('plan', 'extension'), default='plan'); ao.add_argument('--premortem'); ao.add_argument('--plan-review')
    ao.add_argument('--by', required=True); ao.add_argument('--source', required=True); ao.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true')
    wi = sub.add_parser('whatif'); wi.add_argument('--out', required=True)
    pr = sub.add_parser('proposed'); pr.add_argument('--drop')
    rc = sub.add_parser('recompute'); rc.add_argument('--from-linear', action='store_true'); rc.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true')
    sy = sub.add_parser('sync'); sy.add_argument('--decision', action='append'); sy.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true')
    ty = sub.add_parser('tidy'); ty.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true')
    a = p.parse_args()
    if a.cmd == 'add' and any(x is not None and not x.strip() for x in (a.skip_premortem, a.skip_review)):
        die('--skip-premortem / --skip-review need the reason')
    {'list': cmd_list, 'seed': cmd_seed, 'add': cmd_add, 'adopt': cmd_adopt, 'recompute': cmd_recompute, 'sync': cmd_sync,
     'tidy': cmd_tidy, 'whatif': cmd_whatif, 'proposed': cmd_proposed}[a.cmd](a)


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
